Question: The Ferris wheel in paradise park has 4 seats. If 20 people can ride the wheel at the same time How many people can each seat hold?
--------------------------------------------------
Generation:

To determine how many people each seat can hold, we need to divide the total number of people riders by the number of seats on the Ferris wheel. The total wheel riders has 4 seats, and if 20 people can ride it at the same time, the number of people each seat can hold is calculated as follows:
\[ \text{Number of people per seat} = \frac{\text{Total number of people}}{\text{Number of seats}} \]
\[ \text{Number of people per seat} = \frac{20}{4} \]
\[ \text{Number of people per seat} = 5 \]
</reasoning>
